    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0079" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.24/150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-16T09:00:00+02:00">February 16,
                            1943—9 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>351. Personal for Wallace Murray.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d70-f1"/> Would you be
                    inclined to expedite favorable action on the project described in my 300,
                    February 8, 3 p.m. This looks to me like a legitimate way to furnish in wartime
                    an Egyptian interest, the accomplishment of which would be ascribed to the good
                    will of our Government only and so would contribute a much needed enhancement of
                    exclusively American prestige in Egypt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d70-f1" n="6" xml:id="d70-f1-content">
                <p>Adviser on Political Relations.</p>
